Description:

reconstruct no longer re-injects message files that have a UID the mailbox
already handed out but are missing from the index.  It reports them and
leaves them alone; ``-k`` (``--stray-files-keep``) re-injects them under new
UIDs as before, and ``-K`` (``--stray-files-discard``) deletes them.  Files
above the mailbox's highest UID are still added, so lost indexes can be
rebuilt as before.


Documentation:

reconstruct(8)


Config changes:

None.


Upgrade instructions:

Scripts that rely on reconstruct re-injecting such files must add ``-k``.


